      <h3>Learning Objectives</h3>

      <p>
        By the end of this lesson, you should be able to:
      </p>

      <ul class="objective-list">
        <li>
          Identify four important categories of AI tools
          used by developers.
        </li>

        <li>
          Explain the difference between an external
          AI chatbot and a project-aware coding tool.
        </li>

        <li>
          Explain how intelligent code completion works.
        </li>

        <li>
          Describe what coding agents can do across
          multiple project files.
        </li>

        <li>
          Explain how AI code-review tools support
          human reviewers.
        </li>

        <li>
          Select an appropriate AI tool for a specific
          development task.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="important">
        <strong>Central idea:</strong>
        AI development tools do not all perform the same job.
        A responsible developer must understand which tool
        category is suitable for each task.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="english">
      <h2>English Technical Section</h2>

      <p>
        Developers now have access to several types of
        AI-powered tools. Although many of these tools use
        similar AI technology, they interact with developers
        and software projects in different ways.
      </p>

      <p>
        The four important categories covered in this lesson are:
      </p>

      <div class="tool-grid">
        <article class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-number">1</div>

          <h3>External AI Chatbots</h3>

          <p>
            External AI chatbots are general conversation tools.
            Developers can use them to ask questions, learn
            programming concepts, plan projects, analyze short
            code examples, and discuss possible solutions.
          </p>

          <p>
            Examples mentioned in this course include:
          </p>

          <span class="tag">ChatGPT</span>
          <span class="tag">Gemini</span>

          <h4>Good uses</h4>

          <ul>
            <li>Learning a programming concept.</li>
            <li>Planning a new project.</li>
            <li>Explaining an error message.</li>
            <li>Discussing different solution ideas.</li>
            <li>Generating a small example.</li>
          </ul>

          <h4>Main limitation</h4>

          <p>
            A normal external chatbot does not automatically
            know everything inside your local project.
          </p>

          <p>
            It can only work with project information that you
            provide through your message, uploaded files,
            connected services, or another supported method.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-number">2</div>

          <h3>AI Code-Completion Tools</h3>

          <p>
            Code-completion tools work inside or alongside a
            code editor. They examine the current file,
            nearby code, and other available context to predict
            what the developer may want to type next.
          </p>

          <p>
            Examples covered in this course include:
          </p>

          <span class="tag">GitHub Copilot</span>
          <span class="tag">Cursor</span>

          <h4>What makes the completion intelligent?</h4>

          <p>
            Traditional autocomplete may suggest a variable,
            method, or property from a known list.
          </p>

          <p>
            AI-powered completion can often suggest:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>A complete line of code.</li>
            <li>A group of related lines.</li>
            <li>An HTML structure.</li>
            <li>A function based on its name or comment.</li>
            <li>Code that matches the surrounding pattern.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            The developer remains in control and decides
            whether to accept, modify, or reject each suggestion.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-number">3</div>

          <h3>AI Coding Agents</h3>

          <p>
            A coding agent can perform work that is larger than
            a normal autocomplete suggestion.
          </p>

          <p>
            Depending on its permissions and instructions,
            an agent may inspect the project, create files,
            update existing files, search for related code,
            run commands, and attempt to complete a multi-step
            development task.
          </p>

          <p>
            Examples mentioned in the lesson include:
          </p>

          <span class="tag">GitHub Copilot</span>
          <span class="tag">Cursor</span>
          <span class="tag">Claude Code</span>

          <h4>Possible agent tasks</h4>

          <ul>
            <li>Create a complete webpage.</li>
            <li>Update several related files.</li>
            <li>Find where a feature is implemented.</li>
            <li>Repair a bug across a project.</li>
            <li>Add a new component or route.</li>
            <li>Run tests and react to test results.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="warning">
            <strong>Important:</strong>
            An agent can make changes quickly, but speed does
            not guarantee correctness. The developer must
            provide clear instructions and review every
            important change.
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="tool-card">
          <div class="tool-number">4</div>

          <h3>AI Code-Review Tools</h3>

          <p>
            AI code-review tools examine code changes and
            provide feedback before those changes are accepted
            into the main project.
          </p>

          <p>
            They are commonly used with pull requests on
            platforms such as GitHub.
          </p>

          <p>
            Examples mentioned in this lesson include:
          </p>

          <span class="tag">BugBot</span>
          <span class="tag">CodeRabbit</span>

          <h4>What might they detect?</h4>

          <ul>
            <li>Possible bugs.</li>
            <li>Missing error handling.</li>
            <li>Security concerns.</li>
            <li>Repeated code.</li>
            <li>Unclear logic.</li>
            <li>Possible performance problems.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Their feedback can give a human reviewer a useful
            starting point, but it should not automatically
            replace human judgment.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h3>Example: Asking an External Chatbot</h3>

      <p>
        A developer could ask a general chatbot:
      </p>

      <pre><code>Explain the difference between an HTML class and an HTML id.
Give me one simple example of each.</code></pre>

      <p>
        This question does not require the chatbot to understand
        an entire private project. It is a general programming
        question.
      </p>

      <h3>Example: Giving a Coding Agent Instructions</h3>

      <p>
        A developer could instruct a project-aware coding agent:
      </p>

      <pre><code>Inspect the existing registration page.

Add a required preferred-language field with two choices:
English and Somali.

Keep the existing design.
Do not change the payment logic.
Show me the files you changed.</code></pre>

      <p>
        This request relates to a specific project. The agent
        needs access to the relevant project files and must
        understand how they work together.
      </p>

      <div class="success">
        <strong>Professional habit:</strong>
        Give coding agents narrow, clear, testable instructions.
        Review the result before moving to the next task.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="somali" class="somali">
      <h2>Qaybta Farsamada ee Af-Soomaaliga</h2>

      <p>
        Qalabka AI ee ay developers-ku isticmaalaan dhammaantood
        isku shaqo ma qabtaan. Qaar waxay ku habboon yihiin
        su'aalaha guud, qaar waxay kaa caawiyaan qorista code-ka,
        qaarna waxay wax ka beddeli karaan mashruuc dhan.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Chatbot-yada AI ee Dibadda</h3>

      <p>
        Chatbot-yada dibadda sida ChatGPT iyo Gemini waxaa loo
        isticmaali karaa in lagu weydiiyo su'aalo, lagu barto
        fikradaha programming-ka, lagu qorsheeyo mashruuc cusub,
        ama lagu sharxo code yar.
      </p>

      <p>
        Chatbot-ku si toos ah uma garanayo dhammaan faylasha
        mashruucaaga gaarka ah. Wuxuu ku shaqayn karaa keliya
        macluumaadka aad siisay ama aad u oggolaatay inuu arko.
      </p>

      <h4>Waxay ku fiican yihiin:</h4>

      <ul>
        <li>Barashada fikrad cusub.</li>
        <li>Sharaxaadda qalad.</li>
        <li>Qorshaynta mashruuc.</li>
        <li>Samaynta tusaale yar.</li>
        <li>Isbarbardhigga xalal kala duwan.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. Qalabka AI Code Completion</h3>

      <p>
        Qalabkani wuxuu ka shaqeeyaa gudaha code editor-ka.
        Wuxuu eegaa code-ka ku dhow meesha aad joogto, dabadeedna
        wuxuu soo jeediyaa waxa laga yaabo inaad qorto marka xigta.
      </p>

      <p>
        GitHub Copilot iyo Cursor waa tusaalooyin qalabkan ka mid ah.
      </p>

      <p>
        Talooyinka la bixiyo waxay noqon karaan:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Hal eray ama variable.</li>
        <li>Hal sadar oo code ah.</li>
        <li>Dhowr sadar oo code ah.</li>
        <li>Function dhammeystiran.</li>
        <li>Qaab HTML ah oo ku habboon code-ka jira.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Developer-ka ayaa go'aaminaya inuu aqbalo, wax ka beddelo,
        ama diido talada.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Coding Agents</h3>

      <p>
        Coding agent-ku wuxuu qaban karaa hawl ka weyn code
        completion-ka caadiga ah.
      </p>

      <p>
        Wuxuu baadhi karaa mashruuca, samayn karaa faylal cusub,
        wax ka beddeli karaa faylal badan, raadin karaa code la
        xiriira hawsha, mararka qaarkoodna wuxuu ordi karaa
        commands ama tests.
      </p>

      <p>
        GitHub Copilot, Cursor, iyo Claude Code waxay tusaale u
        noqon karaan qalab leh awood agent.
      </p>

      <div class="warning">
        <strong>Digniin:</strong>
        Agent-ku si degdeg ah ayuu wax u beddeli karaa, laakiin
        developer-ku waa inuu si taxaddar leh u hubiyaa
        isbeddellada ka hor inta aan la aqbalin.
      </div>

      <h3>4. Qalabka AI Code Review</h3>

      <p>
        Qalabka code review-ga wuxuu baarayaa isbeddellada lagu
        sameeyay code-ka. Badanaa wuxuu ka shaqeeyaa pull request
        la furay.
      </p>

      <p>
        BugBot iyo CodeRabbit waa tusaalooyin lagu xusay casharkan.
      </p>

      <p>
        Waxay soo sheegi karaan:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Bug suuragal ah.</li>
        <li>Amni-darro suuragal ah.</li>
        <li>Error handling maqan.</li>
        <li>Code isku soo noqnoqday.</li>
        <li>Logic aan caddayn.</li>
        <li>Meel waxqabadku gaabis noqon karo.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        AI review-gu wuxuu caawin karaa qofka code-ka eegaya,
        laakiin kama maarmin hubinta bini'aadamka.
      </p>

      <div class="important">
        <strong>Fikradda muhiimka ah:</strong>
        Dooro qalabka ku habboon hawsha aad qabanayso.
        Ha u isticmaalin hal nooc oo AI ah dhammaan shaqooyinka.
      </div>
