    <section id="comparison">
      <h2 class="comparison-title">
        Tool Category Comparison
      </h2>

      <div class="table-wrapper">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Category</th>
              <th>Main Purpose</th>
              <th>Project Awareness</th>
              <th>Typical Output</th>
              <th>Developer Responsibility</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>

          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>
                External AI Chatbot
              </td>

              <td>
                Answer questions, explain concepts,
                and support planning.
              </td>

              <td>
                Usually limited to information supplied
                or made available by the user.
              </td>

              <td>
                Explanations, suggestions, plans,
                and code examples.
              </td>

              <td>
                Provide enough context and verify the answer.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                AI Code Completion
              </td>

              <td>
                Suggest what the developer may type next.
              </td>

              <td>
                Understands the current file and available
                surrounding context.
              </td>

              <td>
                A word, line, block, function,
                or repeated code pattern.
              </td>

              <td>
                Accept, modify, or reject each suggestion.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                AI Coding Agent
              </td>

              <td>
                Perform larger, multi-step development work.
              </td>

              <td>
                Can inspect and operate across project files
                when access is provided.
              </td>

              <td>
                New files, edited files, commands,
                tests, and completed features.
              </td>

              <td>
                Give clear limits, inspect changes,
                and test the result.
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td>
                AI Code Review
              </td>

              <td>
                Analyze code changes and suggest improvements.
              </td>

              <td>
                Focuses on the changed code and related context.
              </td>

              <td>
                Review comments, warnings,
                and suggested corrections.
              </td>

              <td>
                Decide which findings are correct and important.
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

